      "writtenOn": "2018-08-23T16:53:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The comment at the top is not being contradicted -- This is swapping the flask form of \u003c[type]:[VarName]\u003e to {[VarName]} (example: \u003cstring:user_id\u003e -\u003e {user_id} ). We are just handling the prefix as well in this case not just the entity path.\n\nI can fix the comment here, but tl;dr:\n\nFix the entire url including the prefix, because the prefix may include route substitutions. Otherwise, we end up with something like: /v3/thing/\u003cstring:project_id\u003e/roles/{roles}\n\ninstead of: /v3/thing/{project_id}/roles/{roles}\n\nI could split the string sub part out if it would help.",
      "parentUuid": "3f79a3b5_4e5b6286",
